    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation for databasehandler: Delegates to the pool-taking constructor after resolving the pool from the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file implements the small RAII lease class. The default constructor finds the shared <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" kindref="compound">DatabaseConnectionPool</ref> in the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref> and hands it to the pool-taking constructor, which immediately leases a connection. The destructor returns that connection, and get_connection()/reconnect_all() simply expose the lease or forward a request to the pool.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: It is the implementation behind every synchronous database call: controllers and the watchdog create a <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref>, and these few functions are what actually acquire and release the connection. Because the return to the pool happens in the destructor, exceptions in query code cannot strand a connection. Without this file the lease abstraction would be declared but undefined, so no synchronous request could obtain a connection.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>RAII (acquire in constructor, release in destructor): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Delegating constructors (one constructor calls another): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/initializer_list">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/initializer_list</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::move (transfer ownership without copying): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/move">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/move</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::shared_ptr: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/shared_ptr">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/shared_ptr</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
